Ciao a tutti / Hello everyone,

the weather forecasts for the next 10 days show a strong drop of temperatures=
 in Central and Northern Europe:
max 2-6 degrees in Munich, Zurich, Berlin, Copenhagen, Amsterdam, Geneva, a b=
it milder in Paris, London and Milan.
First snow in Munich is expected around 20 October, snow down to 1,000 m in S=
witzerland.

This is the moment we wait for all year. A few reminders from Retail Excellen=
ce and Merchandising:

HEAVY DOWN FIRST
- Bring the iconic jackets to the front table and the first rail: MAYA, MONTC=
LA, MONTGENEVRE for men; MAIRE,
  HERMINE, FLAMMETTE for women. Where black MAIRE is missing, show beige and =
off-white.
- Remind the client of the warmth rating: the Montgenevre wool shell is the w=
armest city jacket we have.
- ARNEB: our feedback from the first weeks is that it fits generous. Let the =
client try his usual size AND one
  size down, most of them leave with the smaller one.

LAYERING
- Logo Cardigan / Tricot Padded Cardigan under the down jacket: the easiest U=
PT driver.
- Beanie + Cashmere Scarf + Tech Gloves at the cash desk.

STOCK
- Check your depth on beanies and gloves today, not on Saturday. Send repleni=
shment requests to Luca Ferrari's team
  by Wednesday noon for Friday delivery.
- No extra allocation of heavy down is planned before end of October, transfe=
rs between stores only.

CLIENTELING
- Call the clients who looked at a down jacket in September without buying.

Buone vendite!
Matteo & Chiara

